    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Let me confirm the change works end-to-end by reviewing the complete picture.\n\nThe implementation is complete. Here's what I changed to satisfy the spec (\"When no registration date is supplied, set it to the server's current date and return `registrationDate` in ISO format `YYYY-MM-DD`\"):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string`, `format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` inherits from `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, this field flows into both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`, so it can be supplied) and the response DTO (`OwnerDto`, so it's returned). `format: date` generates a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to the new `registration_date` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it by name automatically in both directions.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 The defaulting rule: after mapping the request to an `Owner`, if `registrationDate` is null, set it to `LocalDate.now()` (server's current date). A supplied date passes through untouched.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column (tests use `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema file must declare it; the others updated for consistency).\n\nResults:\n- `coreDefaultsToToday` (no date supplied \u2192 today) \u2705\n- `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (`2020-06-15` supplied \u2192 returned verbatim) \u2705\n- Full suite: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**",
